speechtext:
1.	What was the total production in pounds of pork and beef in each of the years 1943, 1944 and up to July 1, 1945, (a) in Canada as a whole; (b) in Manitoba; (c) in Alberta;
(d)	in Saskatchewan?
2.	What floor prices, if any, have been set on the said products at any time during the present year?

1.	From June 1 to July 31, 1945. what orders were placed by the Department of Munitions and Supply on behalf of the Department of National Defence for, (a) army uniforms and greatcoats; (b) R.C.A.F. uniforms and greatcoats; (e) naval uniforms and greatcoats;
(d)	underwear; (e) hosiery; (f) naval white broadcloth shirts; (g) . R.C.A.F. dress shirts; (h) khaid cloth; (i) naval serge?
2.	What are the names of persons or firms receiving these orders and on what date was each order placed?
